- op: discuss  # 5fd3
  at: '2026-07-30T19:28:26Z'  # 5fd3
  by: agent  # 5fd3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5fd3
  clock: 3  # 5fd3
  nonce: 5fd3  # 5fd3
  message: "WONT_DO — both halves fail on measurement. Re-measured on a fresh self-survey (95 analysis_runs).\n\nHALF 1, 'null on dominant Python pass': FALSE. The python AR's pass_version is a real digest (sha256:cd47efcb5056...), and across ALL 95 ARs, ZERO have a null or empty pass_version. There is no null to fix.\n\nHALF 2, 'implications text references pass_versions absent from captured block': the absence is real — reproducibility_context.captured holds {grammars, hypergumbo_version, python_implementation, python_version, tree_sitter_version} and no pass_versions — but the text is NOT wrong about it. It reads 'matching per-pass code hashes (analysis_runs[].pass_version), hypergumbo_version, ...', i.e. it explicitly cites analysis_runs[] as the location. That IS where the data lives and where it belongs: pass_version is per-run, captured is a single run-wide block, and copying 95 per-run digests into it would mint a second home for the same fact (the duplicate-home the WI-palon ruling declined).\n\nThe residual is a LEGIBILITY nit, not a defect: pass_version is listed alongside four fields that DO live in captured, so a reader skimming may expect all five to be co-located. That justifies neither moving data nor rewriting a citation that is already correct, and it is well below a P1 bar.\n\nClosing wont_do rather than done because there is nothing to fix. Reopening would need a real null pass_version on a real run, which this measurement rules out for the self-corpus."  # 5fd3
